comments.message:
For some reason I did not get notified about this thread, sorry for the late reply. 

> The code to GET systems collection does not have this condition.

True, this check is only needed when doing requests on the ComputerSystem identifier, 
i.e  GET /redfish/v1/Systems/system. 

Single-host expects either default 'system' systemName (= ComputerSystem resource identifier in redfish), or anything that is set via BMCWEB_REDFISH_SYSTEM_URI_NAME. On multi-host, neither of those is expected, the systemName comes from the 'Name' property of the EM configuration that defines the ManagedHost interface. 
That is why the following check exists everywhere we enable multi-host support

`if (!BMCWEB_EXPERIMENTAL_REDFISH_MULTI_COMPUTER_SYSTEM) {
     if (systemName != BMCWEB_REDFISH_SYSTEM_URI_NAME) {
         return ERR;
     }
 }
`

This is only to validate for single-host, on multi-host we don't make assumptions about the systemName used to identify a host, other than the identifiers used for all hosts being unique.
